{"id":"shapes","locale":"fr","nextCourse":"solids","prevCourse":"sequences","title":"Aires et Formes Géométriques","description":"Introduction, Rectangles et Carrés, Parallélogrammes, Triangles, Polygones, Cercles et Circonférence, Aire du Cercle, Résumé des Formules","color":"#0F82F2","level":"Foundations","icon":"/content/shapes/icon.png","hero":"/content/shapes/hero.jpg","goals":11,"sections":[{"id":"introduction","title":"Introduction","url":"/course/shapes/introduction","steps":["intro","perimeter-vs-area","units"],"goals":3,"duration":5},{"id":"rectangles","title":"Rectangles et Carrés","url":"/course/shapes/rectangles","steps":["rectangle-area","rectangle-perimeter","square","rectangle-exercises"],"goals":3,"duration":5},{"id":"parallelograms","title":"Parallélogrammes","url":"/course/shapes/parallelograms","steps":["parallelogram"],"goals":1,"duration":5},{"id":"triangles","title":"Triangles","url":"/course/shapes/triangles","steps":["triangle-area","triangle-example"],"goals":1,"duration":5},{"id":"polygons","title":"Polygones","url":"/course/shapes/polygons","steps":["polygons-intro"],"goals":0,"duration":5},{"id":"circles","title":"Cercles et Circonférence","url":"/course/shapes/circles","steps":["circle-intro","circumference","circumference-example"],"goals":2,"duration":5},{"id":"circle-area","title":"Aire du Cercle","url":"/course/shapes/circle-area","steps":["circle-area","circle-area-example"],"goals":1,"duration":5},{"id":"summary","title":"Résumé des Formules","url":"/course/shapes/summary","steps":["formulas"],"goals":0,"duration":5}],"steps":{"intro":{"id":"intro","title":"Intro","html":"<x-step id=\"intro\" goals=\"\"><div class=\"row padded\"><div class=\"grow\"> <p>Dans la vie quotidienne, nous avons souvent besoin de mesurer des surfaces : la taille d'un appartement, la surface d'un terrain de football, ou la quantité de peinture nécessaire pour un mur.</p><p>L'<strong>aire</strong> d'une figure est la mesure de la surface qu'elle occupe. L'aire s'exprime en unités carrées : cm², m², km²...</p><p>Le <strong>périmètre</strong> d'une figure est la longueur de son contour. Le périmètre s'exprime en unités de longueur : cm, m, km...</p></div><div style=\"width: 300px\"> <x-img src=\"/content/shapes/images/park.jpg\" width=\"300\" height=\"200\"></x-img><p class=\"caption\"> Calculer l'aire d'un parc permet de savoir combien de gazon il faut acheter.</p></div></div> </x-step>","goals":[],"keywords":[]},"perimeter-vs-area":{"id":"perimeter-vs-area","title":"Perimeter Vs Area","html":"<x-step id=\"perimeter-vs-area\" goals=\"blank-0 blank-1 blank-2\"><h2>Périmètre ou Aire ?</h2><p>Dans chaque situation, détermine s'il faut calculer le périmètre ou l'aire :</p><div class=\"row padded\"><div class=\"grow\"> <ol> <li>Pour savoir combien de moquette acheter pour couvrir le sol d'une pièce, on calcule l'<x-blank-mc goal=\"blank-0\"><button class=\"choice\">aire</button><button class=\"choice\">périmètre</button></x-blank-mc> de la pièce.</li></ol> </div><div style=\"width: 200px\"> <x-img width=\"200\" height=\"133\" src=\"/content/shapes/images/carpet.jpg\"></x-img></div></div> <div class=\"row padded\"><div class=\"grow\"> <ol start=\"2\"> <li>Pour savoir quelle longueur de clôture acheter pour entourer un jardin, on calcule le <x-blank-mc goal=\"blank-1\"><button class=\"choice\">périmètre</button><button class=\"choice\">aire</button></x-blank-mc> du jardin.</li></ol> </div><div style=\"width: 200px\"> <x-img width=\"200\" height=\"133\" src=\"/content/shapes/images/fence.jpg\"></x-img></div></div> <div class=\"row padded\"><div class=\"grow\"> <ol start=\"3\"> <li>Pour savoir combien de peinture acheter pour peindre un mur, on calcule l'<x-blank-mc goal=\"blank-2\"><button class=\"choice\">aire</button><button class=\"choice\">périmètre</button></x-blank-mc> du mur.</li></ol> </div><div style=\"width: 200px\"> <x-img width=\"200\" height=\"133\" src=\"/content/shapes/images/paint.jpg\"></x-img></div></div> </x-step>","goals":["blank-0","blank-1","blank-2"],"keywords":[]},"units":{"id":"units","title":"Units","html":"<x-step id=\"units\" goals=\"\"><h2>Unités de mesure</h2><p>Pour mesurer des longueurs, on utilise le <strong>mètre</strong> et ses multiples :</p><ul> <li>1 kilomètre (km) = 1000 mètres</li><li>1 mètre (m) = 100 centimètres</li><li>1 centimètre (cm) = 10 millimètres</li></ul> <p>Pour mesurer des aires, on utilise le <strong>mètre carré</strong> et ses multiples :</p><ul> <li>1 m² = 10 000 cm² (car 100 × 100 = 10 000)</li><li>1 km² = 1 000 000 m² (car 1000 × 1000 = 1 000 000)</li></ul> <p>Un <strong>mètre carré</strong> (m²) est l'aire d'un carré de 1 mètre de côté. Un <strong>centimètre carré</strong> (cm²) est l'aire d'un carré de 1 centimètre de côté.</p></x-step>","goals":[],"keywords":[]},"rectangle-area":{"id":"rectangle-area","title":"Rectangle Area","html":"<x-step id=\"rectangle-area\" goals=\"blank-0\"><h2>Aire d'un rectangle</h2><div class=\"row padded\"><div class=\"grow\"> <p>Pour calculer l'aire d'un rectangle, on peut le remplir de carrés unitaires et les compter.</p><p>Un rectangle de 5 cm de longueur et 3 cm de largeur contient 5 × 3 = <x-blank solution=\"15\" goal=\"blank-0\"></x-blank> carrés d'un centimètre carré.</p><p>Donc l'<strong>aire du rectangle</strong> = longueur × largeur</p><p class=\"text-center\"> <span class=\"math\" data-voice=\"_A_ equals _L_ times _l_\"><mi>A</mi><mo value=\"=\">=</mo><mi>L</mi><mo value=\"×\">×</mo><mi>l</mi></span></p></div><div style=\"width: 280px\"> <x-geopad width=\"280\" height=\"200\"><svg><rect x=\"20\" y=\"20\" width=\"40\" height=\"40\" fill=\"rgba(15,130,242,0.3)\" stroke=\"#0F82F2\"></rect><rect x=\"20\" y=\"60\" width=\"40\" height=\"40\" fill=\"rgba(15,130,242,0.3)\" stroke=\"#0F82F2\"></rect><rect x=\"20\" y=\"100\" width=\"40\" height=\"40\" fill=\"rgba(15,130,242,0.3)\" stroke=\"#0F82F2\"></rect><rect x=\"60\" y=\"20\" width=\"40\" height=\"40\" fill=\"rgba(15,130,242,0.3)\" stroke=\"#0F82F2\"></rect><rect x=\"60\" y=\"60\" width=\"40\" height=\"40\" fill=\"rgba(15,130,242,0.3)\" stroke=\"#0F82F2\"></rect><rect x=\"60\" y=\"100\" width=\"40\" height=\"40\" fill=\"rgba(15,130,242,0.3)\" stroke=\"#0F82F2\"></rect><rect x=\"100\" y=\"20\" width=\"40\" height=\"40\" fill=\"rgba(15,130,242,0.3)\" stroke=\"#0F82F2\"></rect><rect x=\"100\" y=\"60\" width=\"40\" height=\"40\" fill=\"rgba(15,130,242,0.3)\" stroke=\"#0F82F2\"></rect><rect x=\"100\" y=\"100\" width=\"40\" height=\"40\" fill=\"rgba(15,130,242,0.3)\" stroke=\"#0F82F2\"></rect><rect x=\"140\" y=\"20\" width=\"40\" height=\"40\" fill=\"rgba(15,130,242,0.3)\" stroke=\"#0F82F2\"></rect><rect x=\"140\" y=\"60\" width=\"40\" height=\"40\" fill=\"rgba(15,130,242,0.3)\" stroke=\"#0F82F2\"></rect><rect x=\"140\" y=\"100\" width=\"40\" height=\"40\" fill=\"rgba(15,130,242,0.3)\" stroke=\"#0F82F2\"></rect><rect x=\"180\" y=\"20\" width=\"40\" height=\"40\" fill=\"rgba(15,130,242,0.3)\" stroke=\"#0F82F2\"></rect><rect x=\"180\" y=\"60\" width=\"40\" height=\"40\" fill=\"rgba(15,130,242,0.3)\" stroke=\"#0F82F2\"></rect><rect x=\"180\" y=\"100\" width=\"40\" height=\"40\" fill=\"rgba(15,130,242,0.3)\" stroke=\"#0F82F2\"></rect><path class=\"blue\" x=\"polygon(point(20,20),point(220,20),point(220,140),point(20,140))\" stroke-width=\"2\"></path></svg></x-geopad></div></div> </x-step>","goals":["blank-0"],"keywords":[]},"rectangle-perimeter":{"id":"rectangle-perimeter","title":"Rectangle Perimeter","html":"<x-step id=\"rectangle-perimeter\" goals=\"\"><h2>Périmètre d'un rectangle</h2><div class=\"row padded\"><div class=\"grow\"> <p>Le périmètre d'un rectangle est la somme des longueurs de ses quatre côtés.</p><p>Un rectangle a deux longueurs égales et deux largeurs égales.</p><p>Donc le <strong>périmètre du rectangle</strong> = 2 × longueur + 2 × largeur</p><p class=\"text-center\"> <span class=\"math\" data-voice=\"_P_ equals 2 _L_ plus 2 _l_\"><mi>P</mi><mo value=\"=\">=</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>L</mi><mo value=\"+\">+</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>l</mi></span> ou <span class=\"math\" data-voice=\"_P_ equals 2 _L_ plus _l_\"><mi>P</mi><mo value=\"=\">=</mo><mn>2</mn><mfenced open=\"(\" close=\")\"><mi>L</mi><mo value=\"+\">+</mo><mi>l</mi></mfenced></span></p></div><div style=\"width: 280px\"> <x-geopad width=\"280\" height=\"180\"><svg><circle name=\"a\" x=\"point(30,30)\"></circle><circle name=\"b\" x=\"point(250,30)\"></circle><circle name=\"c\" x=\"point(250,150)\"></circle><circle name=\"d\" x=\"point(30,150)\"></circle><path class=\"blue\" x=\"segment(a,b)\" label=\"L\"></path><path class=\"red\" x=\"segment(b,c)\" label=\"l\"></path><path class=\"blue\" x=\"segment(c,d)\" label=\"L\"></path><path class=\"red\" x=\"segment(d,a)\" label=\"l\"></path></svg></x-geopad></div></div> </x-step>","goals":[],"keywords":[]},"square":{"id":"square","title":"Square","html":"<x-step id=\"square\" goals=\"\"><h2>Le carré</h2><p>Un carré est un rectangle particulier dont tous les côtés sont égaux.</p><div class=\"row padded\"><div class=\"grow\"> <p>Si le côté du carré mesure <em>c</em>, alors :</p><ul> <li><strong>Aire du carré</strong> = côté × côté = c²</li><li><strong>Périmètre du carré</strong> = 4 × côté = 4c</li></ul> </div><div style=\"width: 200px\"> <x-geopad width=\"200\" height=\"200\"><svg><circle name=\"a\" x=\"point(20,20)\"></circle><circle name=\"b\" x=\"point(180,20)\"></circle><circle name=\"c\" x=\"point(180,180)\"></circle><circle name=\"d\" x=\"point(20,180)\"></circle><path class=\"blue\" x=\"polygon(a,b,c,d)\"></path><path class=\"blue\" x=\"segment(a,b)\" label=\"c\"></path><path class=\"blue\" x=\"segment(b,c)\" label=\"c\"></path></svg></x-geopad></div></div> </x-step>","goals":[],"keywords":[]},"rectangle-exercises":{"id":"rectangle-exercises","title":"Rectangle Exercises","html":"<x-step id=\"rectangle-exercises\" goals=\"blank-0 blank-1\"><h2>Exercices</h2><p class=\"text-center\"> Un rectangle mesure 8 cm de longueur et 5 cm de largeur.</p><p>Son aire est : <span class=\"math\" data-voice=\"8 times 5 equals\"><mn>8</mn><mo value=\"×\">×</mo><mn>5</mn><mo value=\"=\">=</mo></span> <x-blank solution=\"40\" goal=\"blank-0\"></x-blank> cm²</p><p>Son périmètre est : <span class=\"math\" data-voice=\"2 times 8 plus 5 equals\"><mn>2</mn><mo value=\"×\">×</mo><mfenced open=\"(\" close=\")\"><mn>8</mn><mo value=\"+\">+</mo><mn>5</mn></mfenced><mo value=\"=\">=</mo></span> <x-blank solution=\"26\" goal=\"blank-1\"></x-blank> cm</p></x-step>","goals":["blank-0","blank-1"],"keywords":[]},"parallelogram":{"id":"parallelogram","title":"Parallelogram","html":"<x-step id=\"parallelogram\" goals=\"blank-0\"><p>Un <strong>parallélogramme</strong> est un quadrilatère dont les côtés opposés sont parallèles.</p><div class=\"row padded\"><div class=\"grow\"> <p>Pour calculer l'aire d'un parallélogramme, on peut le transformer en rectangle :</p><ol> <li>On \"coupe\" un triangle à droite</li><li>On le \"colle\" à gauche</li><li>On obtient un rectangle !</li></ol> <p>L'<strong>aire du parallélogramme</strong> = base × hauteur</p><p class=\"text-center\"> <span class=\"math\" data-voice=\"_A_ equals _b_ times _h_\"><mi>A</mi><mo value=\"=\">=</mo><mi>b</mi><mo value=\"×\">×</mo><mi>h</mi></span></p><p>Attention : la hauteur est <x-blank-mc goal=\"blank-0\"><button class=\"choice\">perpendiculaire</button><button class=\"choice\">parallèle</button><button class=\"choice\">égale</button></x-blank-mc> à la base !</p></div><div style=\"width: 300px\"> <x-geopad width=\"300\" height=\"200\"><svg><circle name=\"a\" x=\"point(40,150)\"></circle><circle name=\"b\" x=\"point(260,150)\"></circle><circle name=\"c\" x=\"point(220,50)\"></circle><circle name=\"d\" x=\"point(0,50)\"></circle><path class=\"fill blue light\" x=\"polygon(a,b,c,d)\"></path><path class=\"blue\" x=\"polygon(a,b,c,d)\"></path><path class=\"red\" x=\"segment(d,a)\" label=\"h\" arrows=\"both\"></path><path class=\"green\" x=\"segment(a,b)\" label=\"b\"></path></svg></x-geopad></div></div> </x-step>","goals":["blank-0"],"keywords":[]},"triangle-area":{"id":"triangle-area","title":"Triangle Area","html":"<x-step id=\"triangle-area\" goals=\"\"><h2>Aire d'un triangle</h2><div class=\"row padded\"><div class=\"grow\"> <p>Un triangle est la moitié d'un parallélogramme (ou d'un rectangle).</p><p>Si on double un triangle, on obtient un parallélogramme d'aire base × hauteur.</p><p>Donc l'<strong>aire du triangle</strong> = (base × hauteur) ÷ 2</p><p class=\"text-center\"> <span class=\"math\" data-voice=\"_A_ equals _b_ times _h_ over 2\"><mi>A</mi><mo value=\"=\">=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo value=\"×\">×</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></span></p></div><div style=\"width: 300px\"> <x-geopad width=\"300\" height=\"200\"><svg><circle name=\"a\" x=\"point(150,30)\"></circle><circle name=\"b\" x=\"point(40,170)\"></circle><circle name=\"c\" x=\"point(260,170)\"></circle><path class=\"fill red light\" x=\"triangle(a,b,c)\"></path><path class=\"red\" x=\"triangle(a,b,c)\"></path><path class=\"blue dashed\" x=\"segment(a,point(150,170))\" label=\"h\"></path><path class=\"green\" x=\"segment(b,c)\" label=\"b\"></path></svg></x-geopad></div></div> </x-step>","goals":[],"keywords":[]},"triangle-example":{"id":"triangle-example","title":"Triangle Example","html":"<x-step id=\"triangle-example\" goals=\"blank-0\"><h2>Exemple</h2><p class=\"text-center\"> Un triangle a une base de 6 cm et une hauteur de 4 cm.</p><p>Son aire est : <span class=\"math\" data-voice=\"6 times 4 ÷ 2 equals\"><mfenced open=\"(\" close=\")\"><mn>6</mn><mo value=\"×\">×</mo><mn>4</mn></mfenced><mo value=\"÷\">÷</mo><mn>2</mn><mo value=\"=\">=</mo></span> <x-blank solution=\"12\" goal=\"blank-0\"></x-blank> cm²</p></x-step>","goals":["blank-0"],"keywords":[]},"polygons-intro":{"id":"polygons-intro","title":"Polygons Intro","html":"<x-step id=\"polygons-intro\" goals=\"\"><p>Un <strong>polygone</strong> est une figure plane fermée délimitée par des segments de droite.</p><div class=\"row padded\"><div style=\"width: 180px\"> <x-geopad width=\"180\" height=\"150\"><svg><circle name=\"a\" x=\"point(90,20)\"></circle><circle name=\"b\" x=\"point(160,80)\"></circle><circle name=\"c\" x=\"point(140,140)\"></circle><circle name=\"d\" x=\"point(40,140)\"></circle><circle name=\"e\" x=\"point(20,80)\"></circle><path class=\"fill blue light\" x=\"polygon(a,b,c,d,e)\"></path><path class=\"blue\" x=\"polygon(a,b,c,d,e)\"></path></svg></x-geopad><p class=\"caption\"> Pentagone (5 côtés)</p></div><div style=\"width: 180px\"> <x-geopad width=\"180\" height=\"150\"><svg><circle name=\"a1\" x=\"point(90,20)\"></circle><circle name=\"b1\" x=\"point(160,50)\"></circle><circle name=\"c1\" x=\"point(160,110)\"></circle><circle name=\"d1\" x=\"point(90,140)\"></circle><circle name=\"e1\" x=\"point(20,110)\"></circle><circle name=\"f1\" x=\"point(20,50)\"></circle><path class=\"fill green light\" x=\"polygon(a1,b1,c1,d1,e1,f1)\"></path><path class=\"green\" x=\"polygon(a1,b1,c1,d1,e1,f1)\"></path></svg></x-geopad><p class=\"caption\"> Hexagone (6 côtés)</p></div><div style=\"width: 180px\"> <x-geopad width=\"180\" height=\"150\"><svg><circle name=\"a2\" x=\"point(90,15)\"></circle><circle name=\"b2\" x=\"point(145,35)\"></circle><circle name=\"c2\" x=\"point(165,90)\"></circle><circle name=\"d2\" x=\"point(145,140)\"></circle><circle name=\"e2\" x=\"point(90,155)\"></circle><circle name=\"f2\" x=\"point(35,140)\"></circle><circle name=\"g2\" x=\"point(15,90)\"></circle><circle name=\"h2\" x=\"point(35,35)\"></circle><path class=\"fill orange light\" x=\"polygon(a2,b2,c2,d2,e2,f2,g2,h2)\"></path><path class=\"orange\" x=\"polygon(a2,b2,c2,d2,e2,f2,g2,h2)\"></path></svg></x-geopad><p class=\"caption\"> Octogone (8 côtés)</p></div></div> <p>Un polygone <strong>régulier</strong> a tous ses côtés égaux et tous ses angles égaux.</p></x-step>","goals":[],"keywords":[]},"circle-intro":{"id":"circle-intro","title":"Circle Intro","html":"<x-step id=\"circle-intro\" goals=\"blank-0\"><h2>Le cercle</h2><div class=\"row padded\"><div class=\"grow\"> <p>Un <strong>cercle</strong> est l'ensemble des points situés à égale distance d'un point central appelé le <strong>centre</strong>.</p><p>Cette distance constante s'appelle le <strong>rayon</strong> (<em>r</em>).</p><p>Le <strong>diamètre</strong> (<em>d</em>) est un segment qui passe par le centre et relie deux points du cercle. Le diamètre est <x-blank-mc goal=\"blank-0\"><button class=\"choice\">deux fois</button><button class=\"choice\">égal à</button><button class=\"choice\">la moitié du</button></x-blank-mc> le rayon.</p><p class=\"text-center\"> <span class=\"math\" data-voice=\"_d_ equals 2 _r_\"><mi>d</mi><mo value=\"=\">=</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>r</mi></span></p></div><div style=\"width: 280px\"> <x-geopad width=\"280\" height=\"280\"><svg><circle name=\"o\" x=\"point(140,140)\"></circle><circle name=\"p\" x=\"point(240,140)\"></circle><circle name=\"q\" x=\"point(40,140)\"></circle><path class=\"blue\" x=\"circle(o,100)\"></path><path class=\"red\" x=\"segment(o,p)\" label=\"r\"></path><path class=\"green\" x=\"segment(q,p)\" label=\"d\"></path><circle class=\"red\" x=\"o\" label=\"O\"></circle></svg></x-geopad></div></div> </x-step>","goals":["blank-0"],"keywords":[]},"circumference":{"id":"circumference","title":"Circumference","html":"<x-step id=\"circumference\" goals=\"\"><h2>Périmètre du cercle (circonférence)</h2><p>Le périmètre d'un cercle s'appelle la <strong>circonférence</strong>.</p><p>Les mathématiciens ont découvert que le rapport entre la circonférence et le diamètre est toujours le même, quel que soit le cercle. Ce nombre s'appelle <strong>Pi</strong> (π).</p><p class=\"text-center\"> <span class=\"math\"></span></p><p>La <strong>circonférence</strong> = π × diamètre = 2 × π × rayon</p><p class=\"text-center\"> <span class=\"math\" data-voice=\"_C_ equals pi times _d_ equals 2 πr\"><mi>C</mi><mo value=\"=\">=</mo><mi>π</mi><mo value=\"×\">×</mo><mi>d</mi><mo value=\"=\">=</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>πr</mi></span></p></x-step>","goals":[],"keywords":[]},"circumference-example":{"id":"circumference-example","title":"Circumference Example","html":"<x-step id=\"circumference-example\" goals=\"blank-0\"><h2>Exemple</h2><p class=\"text-center\"> Un cercle a un rayon de 5 cm.</p><p>Sa circonférence est : <span class=\"math\" data-voice=\"2 times pi times 5 equals 10 pi ≈\"><mn>2</mn><mo value=\"×\">×</mo><mi>π</mi><mo value=\"×\">×</mo><mn>5</mn><mo value=\"=\">=</mo><mn>10</mn><mi>π</mi><mo value=\"≈\">≈</mo></span> <x-blank solution=\"31,4\" goal=\"blank-0\"></x-blank> cm (arrondi au dixième)</p></x-step>","goals":["blank-0"],"keywords":[]},"circle-area":{"id":"circle-area","title":"Circle Area","html":"<x-step id=\"circle-area\" goals=\"\"><h2>Aire d'un disque</h2><div class=\"row padded\"><div class=\"grow\"> <p>Pour trouver l'aire d'un disque (l'intérieur d'un cercle), on peut le découper en secteurs et les réarranger pour former approximativement un rectangle.</p><p>Plus on découpe de secteurs, plus la forme ressemble à un rectangle de :</p><ul> <li>largeur = rayon (<em>r</em>)</li><li>longueur = moitié de la circonférence = πr</li></ul> <p>L'<strong>aire du disque</strong> = π × rayon²</p><p class=\"text-center\"> <span class=\"math\"></span></p></div><div style=\"width: 280px\"> <x-geopad width=\"280\" height=\"280\"><svg><circle name=\"o\" x=\"point(140,140)\"></circle><path class=\"fill blue light\" x=\"circle(o,100)\"></path><path class=\"blue\" x=\"circle(o,100)\"></path></svg></x-geopad></div></div> </x-step>","goals":[],"keywords":[]},"circle-area-example":{"id":"circle-area-example","title":"Circle Area Example","html":"<x-step id=\"circle-area-example\" goals=\"blank-0\"><h2>Exemple</h2><p class=\"text-center\"> Un disque a un rayon de 3 cm.</p><p>Son aire est : <span class=\"math\"></span> <x-blank solution=\"28,3\" goal=\"blank-0\"></x-blank> cm² (arrondi au dixième)</p></x-step>","goals":["blank-0"],"keywords":[]},"formulas":{"id":"formulas","title":"Formulas","html":"<x-step id=\"formulas\" goals=\"\"><table> <thead> <tr> <th>Figure</th><th>Aire</th><th>Périmètre</th></tr> </thead> <tbody><tr> <td>Rectangle</td><td><span class=\"math\" data-voice=\"_L_ times _l_\"><mi>L</mi><mo value=\"×\">×</mo><mi>l</mi></span></td><td><span class=\"math\" data-voice=\"2 _L_ plus _l_\"><mn>2</mn><mfenced open=\"(\" close=\")\"><mi>L</mi><mo value=\"+\">+</mo><mi>l</mi></mfenced></span></td></tr> <tr> <td>Carré</td><td><span class=\"math\"></span></td><td><span class=\"math\" data-voice=\"4 _c_\"><mn>4</mn><mi>c</mi></span></td></tr> <tr> <td>Parallélogramme</td><td><span class=\"math\" data-voice=\"_b_ times _h_\"><mi>b</mi><mo value=\"×\">×</mo><mi>h</mi></span></td><td>Somme des côtés</td></tr> <tr> <td>Triangle</td><td><span class=\"math\" data-voice=\"_b_ times _h_ over 2\"><mfrac><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo value=\"×\">×</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></span></td><td>Somme des côtés</td></tr> <tr> <td>Cercle/Disque</td><td><span class=\"math\"></span></td><td><span class=\"math\" data-voice=\"2 πr\"><mn>2</mn><mi>πr</mi></span></td></tr> </tbody></table> </x-step>","goals":[],"keywords":[]}},"availableLocales":["fr"],"biosJSON":"{}","glossJSON":"{}","hintsJSON":"{\"welcome\":\"<p>Bienvenue chez Mathigon ! Je suis Archie, ton tuteur personnel. <img class=\\\"emoji\\\" width=\\\"20\\\" height=\\\"20\\\" src=\\\"https://static.mathigon.org/emoji/graduation-cap.png\\\" alt=\\\"graduation-cap\\\"></p>\",\"account\":\"<p>Vous pouvez créer un compte gratuit pour enregistrer vos progrès.</p>\",\"tutorial1\":\"<p>Notre contenu est divisé en petites étapes. Vous devez compléter les activités pour révéler la suite.</p>\",\"tutorial2\":\"<p>Nous enregistrerons tous vos progrès afin que vous puissiez revenir plus tard et continuer là où vous l'avez laissé.</p>\",\"correct\":[\"<p>Bien joué <img class=\\\"emoji\\\" width=\\\"20\\\" height=\\\"20\\\" src=\\\"https://static.mathigon.org/emoji/smiling-face.png\\\" alt=\\\"smiling-face\\\"></p>\",\"<p>Bon travail ! <img class=\\\"emoji\\\" width=\\\"20\\\" height=\\\"20\\\" src=\\\"https://static.mathigon.org/emoji/relieved-face.png\\\" alt=\\\"relieved-face\\\"></p>\",\"<p>Brilliant <img class=\\\"emoji\\\" width=\\\"20\\\" height=\\\"20\\\" src=\\\"https://static.mathigon.org/emoji/thumbs-up.png\\\" alt=\\\"thumbs-up\\\"></p>\",\"<p>Excellent ! <img class=\\\"emoji\\\" width=\\\"20\\\" height=\\\"20\\\" src=\\\"https://static.mathigon.org/emoji/ok-hand.png\\\" alt=\\\"ok-hand\\\"></p>\",\"<p>Cool <img class=\\\"emoji\\\" width=\\\"20\\\" height=\\\"20\\\" src=\\\"https://static.mathigon.org/emoji/smiling-face-with-sunglasses.png\\\" alt=\\\"smiling-face-with-sunglasses\\\"></p>\",\"<p>Agréable ! <img class=\\\"emoji\\\" width=\\\"20\\\" height=\\\"20\\\" src=\\\"https://static.mathigon.org/emoji/victory-hand.png\\\" alt=\\\"victory-hand\\\"></p>\",\"<p>Marche à suivre ! <img class=\\\"emoji\\\" width=\\\"20\\\" height=\\\"20\\\" src=\\\"https://static.mathigon.org/emoji/smiling-face-with-smiling-eyes.png\\\" alt=\\\"smiling-face-with-smiling-eyes\\\"></p>\",\"<p>Exceptionnel <img class=\\\"emoji\\\" width=\\\"20\\\" height=\\\"20\\\" src=\\\"https://static.mathigon.org/emoji/grinning-face.png\\\" alt=\\\"grinning-face\\\"></p>\",\"<p>Superbe ! <img class=\\\"emoji\\\" width=\\\"20\\\" height=\\\"20\\\" src=\\\"https://static.mathigon.org/emoji/star.png\\\" alt=\\\"star\\\"></p>\",\"<p>Merveilleux ! <img class=\\\"emoji\\\" width=\\\"20\\\" height=\\\"20\\\" src=\\\"https://static.mathigon.org/emoji/smiling-face.png\\\" alt=\\\"smiling-face\\\"></p>\"],\"incorrect\":[\"<p>Ce n'est pas tout à fait juste <img class=\\\"emoji\\\" width=\\\"20\\\" height=\\\"20\\\" src=\\\"https://static.mathigon.org/emoji/frowning-face.png\\\" alt=\\\"frowning-face\\\"></p>\",\"<p>Êtes-vous sûr de cela ? <img class=\\\"emoji\\\" width=\\\"20\\\" height=\\\"20\\\" src=\\\"https://static.mathigon.org/emoji/thinking-face.png\\\" alt=\\\"thinking-face\\\"></p>\",\"<p>Cela ne semble pas juste. <img class=\\\"emoji\\\" width=\\\"20\\\" height=\\\"20\\\" src=\\\"https://static.mathigon.org/emoji/hushed-face.png\\\" alt=\\\"hushed-face\\\"></p>\",\"<p>Réessayez ! <img class=\\\"emoji\\\" width=\\\"20\\\" height=\\\"20\\\" src=\\\"https://static.mathigon.org/emoji/confused-face.png\\\" alt=\\\"confused-face\\\"></p>\"],\"welcomeMorning\":\"<p>Bonjour !</p>\",\"welcomeAfternoon\":\"<p>Bonjour !</p>\",\"welcomeEvening\":\"<p>Bonsoir !</p>\",\"welcomeMorningNamed\":\"<p>Bonjour, $name !</p>\",\"welcomeAfternoonNamed\":\"<p>Bonjour, $name !</p>\",\"welcomeEveningNamed\":\"<p>Bonsoir, $name !</p>\",\"serverError\":\"<p>Désolé, je ne peux pas aider pour le moment. Vérifiez votre connexion Internet ou réessayez plus tard. <img class=\\\"emoji\\\" width=\\\"20\\\" height=\\\"20\\\" src=\\\"https://static.mathigon.org/emoji/confused-face.png\\\" alt=\\\"confused-face\\\"></p>\",\"polygon-regular\":\"<p>This shape is a <strong>regular</strong> polygon because all sides are the same length.</p>\",\"not-polygon-curved\":\"<p>This shape is <strong>not</strong> a polygon because it has curved sides.</p>\",\"not-polygon-hole\":\"<p>This shape is <strong>not</strong> a polygon because it has a hole.</p>\",\"polygon-irregular\":\"<p>This shape is an <strong>irregular</strong> polygon because the side lengths are not all the same.</p>\",\"not-polygon-closed\":\"<p>This shape is <strong>not</strong> a polygon because it is not closed.</p>\",\"not-polygon-crossing\":\"<p>This shape is <strong>not</strong> a polygon because two of the edges cross over each other.</p>\",\"polygon-voronoi\":\"<p>This is an <strong>irregular</strong> polygon from the Voronoi diagram above. We’ll find the area of it below.</p>\",\"canada\":\"<p>The leaf has some curved sections, so while not technically a polygon, it closely resembles a 25-sided polygon. This is called a icosikaipentagon!</p>\",\"south-africa\":\"<p>While it may not initially look like it, the yellow and while shapes in the flag are both hexagons!</p>\",\"finland\":\"<p>The blue polygon has 12 sides and is called a dodecagon.</p>\",\"nepal\":\"<p>The flag itself is a pentagon and the bottom image inside the flag is a 24-sided polygon called a icositetragon.</p>\"}"}